' 9. Add friend (request → accept)
' Use case: Add friend (Friends & communicate) · Actors: Learner A, Learner B
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Observer (publish/subscribe): after each change, publish() sends events through the RealtimeBus (PostgreSQL
'     LISTEN/NOTIFY when several API processes run) to the other learner's open event stream
'     (services/realtime.service.ts, web lib/realtime.ts useRealtime)
'   - Unit of work: each change (request, notification) is one transaction; events are published only after commit
'     (friend.service.ts change())
'   - Repository
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens and outside services, «control» use-case logic (controllers,
' services, and the adapter interfaces in front of outside services), «entity» stored data (repository, stores);
' the database keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 09 Add friend
title 9. Add friend (request → accept)
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Learner A" as A
boundary "Web app A" as WebA
control "Friend controller" as Ctrl
control "Friend service" as Svc
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB
control "Live updates\n(RealtimeBus)" as Bus
boundary "Web app B" as WebB
actor "Learner B" as B

note over Bus, WebB : «Observer»: B's open tabs subscribe to B's event stream

A -> WebA : enter B's username → Add friend
WebA -> Ctrl : POST /api/friends/requests
Ctrl -> Svc : sendFriendRequest(username)
Svc -> Repo : B exists, not blocked, accepts requests? limits OK?
alt not allowed
  Svc --> WebA : 403 / 409 / 429 with the reason
end
group «Unit of work» withTransaction()
  Svc -> Repo : save pending request
  Svc -> Repo : notification for B
  Repo -> DB : INSERT …
end
Svc -> Bus : publish(B, "friend request")
Bus --> WebB : event
WebB --> B : bell count + request shown at once
Ctrl --> WebA : "Request sent"

B -> WebB : Accept
WebB -> Ctrl : PUT /api/friends/requests/:id (accept: true)
Ctrl -> Svc : respondToFriendRequest()
alt accept
  group «Unit of work» withTransaction()
    Svc -> Repo : status accepted, notification for A
    Repo -> DB : UPDATE / INSERT
  end
  Svc -> Bus : publish(A, "accepted")
  Bus --> WebA : event
  WebA --> A : "You and B are now friends"
  Svc -> Svc : check friend achievements for A and B (Study Buddy)
else decline
  Svc -> Repo : status declined
  Svc -> Bus : publish(A, "updated")
  Bus --> WebA : request leaves A's list (A isn't told why)
end
@enduml
